			],
			"Message": "docs(Project): Initialize comprehensive system architecture documentation\n\nAdd a new suite of foundational documentation to `Documentation/GitHub/` covering the complete Land editor architecture, build pipeline, editor core adaptation, inter-component protocols, polyfills, and Rust infrastructure.\n\nCreate the following seven new documents:\n- `Architecture.md`: System architecture, process model, IPC patterns, and service layer design.\n- `BuildPipeline.md`: Multi-stage build flow, environment propagation, profile system, and artifact layout.\n- `EditorCore.md`: Wind service layer architecture, workbench variants, and command dispatch logic.\n- `InterComponentProtocol.md`: Tauri IPC, Vine gRPC, Spine protocol, and connection lifecycle management.\n- `Polyfills.md`: Preload shims, SkyBridge, Cocoon initialization, and worker service worker logic.\n- `RustInfrastructure.md`: Details on Common, Echo, Mountain, Mist, Air, Rest, SideCar, and Grove.\n- `Workflow.md`: Updated to index the new system documentation and per-element architecture links.\n\nSynchronize the `Element` submodule to include standardized `Architecture.md` files with Mermaid diagrams across 13 core components (Air, Common, Echo, Mountain, etc.). Update `turbo.json` to add `DebugServer` and `Inspect` to the whitelist.\n\nThis establishes a unified technical reference clarifying the separation of concerns between the Rust backend, TypeScript services, and UI layers.",
			"SHA": "a19914cf8910a2c46425fc8252a9c8baa824cd67"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-05-15T21:37:57Z",
			"File": [
				"⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				119,
				1
			],
			"Message": "chore(Element): Update submodule to expose bridge metadata and enable cross-frame diagnostics\n\nSynchronize the Element submodule from 29862a1a to 7c04c5a9 to integrate observability enhancements for the UI bridging pipeline between the Sky component layer and the extension host.\n\nIn Sky, refactor `_InstallSkyBridgeOnce` to expose execution metadata via `globalThis` using `__CEL_LAST_SET_HTML_INFO__` and `__CEL_LATEST_SET_HTML_INFO__`, capturing view state and timestamps for `set-html` operations to enable external debug inspection. Additionally, standardize line breaks in `window.confirm` and `window.prompt` strings for consistent dialog formatting.\n\nIn Output, extend the `RuntimeDiagnostics` transform plugin to leverage the new global metadata. Inject listeners for cross-frame `postMessage` traffic (capped at 50 events) and scheduled checks for the Sky bridge globals to report `SKY_SET_HTML` and `SKY_FIRST_SET_HTML` lifecycle events.\n\nThese changes provide granular telemetry for debugging UI communication and state synchronization issues within extension webviews.",
			"SHA": "eab3041fbe5dadfd16e7eb8530791ebcc707d4ca"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-05-15T21:36:26Z",
			"File": [
				"⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				119,
				1
			],
			"Message": "chore(Element): Synchronize Element submodule with new Output diagnostics\n\nUpdate the Element submodule from 436dcbfa to 29862a1a to integrate the `feat(Output)` addition of comprehensive runtime diagnostics.\n\nThe new commit injects a diagnostic script into the webview content pipeline that performs periodic DOM state checks (every 500ms), monitors React hook status, captures full DOM snapshots, and verifies `acquireVsCodeApi` availability. These telemetry features are scoped to the first 30 seconds of the session to aid debugging of rendering issues and API availability in custom environments via the `RuntimeDiagnosticsInner` transform plugin in Rest.\n\nAligning with the previous commit standardizing escaped quotes in webview logging, this update ensures the build pipeline provides deeper observability for the extension host and UI runtime.",
			"SHA": "7732f3f163cb562924e06159917926e93558eba9"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-05-15T21:34:26Z",
			"File": [
				"⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				119,
				1
			],
			"Message": "fix(Output): Standardize escaped quotes in webview logging diagnostics\n\nCorrect the escaping of quote characters within the injected `DEBUG_WV` logging call in `Source/Plugin/Transform/Inject/Webview/Debug/Logging.ts`.\n\nReplace double-escaped quotes (`\\\"`) with single-escaped quotes (`\"`) for the `id=\"root\"` and `type=\"module\"` string checks. This ensures the generated JavaScript string literals are syntactically correct, allowing the runtime diagnostics to properly identify the React root element and module scripts during webview content processing in the Rest bundler pipeline.",
			"SHA": "5e7fe39ce66f8b985b397be4bfd625f99d80a37a"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-05-15T21:32:50Z",
			"File": [
				"⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				119,
				1
			],
			"Message": "chore(Element): Synchronize 3 submodules for gRPC stability and naming standardization\n\nUpdate the core extension host and backend submodules to address cold-start connectivity issues and enforce strict PascalCase configuration naming.\n\n**Cocoon**: Implement asynchronous polling in the `Service.ts` health check to wait for gRPC channel readiness (up to 3s) before validation. Replace the immediate synchronous state check to prevent false positives during channel transitions (IDLE/CONNECTING) and ensure robust handshake timing with Mountain.\n\n**Mountain**: Standardize WKWebView debug server configuration keys in `Info.plist` and Rust sources from `DEBUG_SERVER` to `DebugServer` and `DebugServerPort` per project naming conventions. Remove the deprecated `DisableUIFixes` key and clear the `Trace` value to reduce release profile noise.\n\n**Output**: Regenerate build artifacts and update the `DisableUIFixes` toggle logic and webview diagnostics logging to align with the latest upstream changes in the `Output` pipeline, ensuring consistent build artifact generation across the extension host.\n\nThese changes stabilize the gRPC bootstrap sequence for the extension host and ensure all native and build configuration keys adhere to the PascalCase standard.",
			"SHA": "bc736a634c5899248ee91dd91addf38b39bbb8ea"
		}
	],
